    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Joint Sitting under Article 108 is summoned by the President and presided over by the Speaker of the Lok Sabha.",
        "Money Bills can only be introduced in the Lok Sabha with the prior recommendation of the President.",
        "Rajya Sabha is a permanent house and cannot be dissolved, whereas Lok Sabha has a normal term of 5 years."
      ],
